PixelMatte is a breakthrough in image matting: it fine-tunes pixel-space diffusion Transformers (like HiDream-8B) to cut out hair and transparent edges with stunning precision—no extra decoders, no paired image-to-image training required.

Directly operating on RGB pixels, PixelMatte slashes error rates by 30–44% over RenderMatte on real-image benchmarks (P3M-500-NP, AM-2K) and matches SOTA on synthetics, all in a single fast pass at up to 2K resolution. Two tiny calibration modules—LayerShift and a 1.3M High-Pass Refiner—handle regional opacity and edge sharpness.

This is the first time a text-to-image diffusion model has been repurposed as a high-fidelity matting engine with just minimal tuning, opening the door to using pixel diffusion models for precision-demanding vision tasks everywhere from AR to VFX.

